        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fourier Analysis - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Why complex exponentials?**: They're eigenfunctions of differentiation (and LTI systems).\nIf you input e^{jωt} to an LTI system, output is H(jω)·e^{jωt} — same frequency, scaled."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-FOURIER-ANALYSIS.md#017",
      "path": [
        "01-FOURIER-ANALYSIS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
