        "root_concepts": "[fourier, analysis]",
        "section": "signal-processing",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Fourier Analysis - A Layered Guide",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Key properties**:\n- Linearity: F{ax+by} = aX + bY\n- Time shift: F{x(t-t₀)} = e^{-jωt₀}·X(jω)  (phase rotation, same magnitude)\n- Frequency shift: F{e^{jω₀t}x(t)} = X(j(ω-ω₀))  (modulation theorem)\n- **Convolution ↔ Multiplication**: F{x★h} = X(jω)·H(jω)  (fundamental)\n- Time scaling: F{x(at)} = (1/|a|)·X(jω/a)  (compress time → expand frequency)\n- Differentiation: F{x'(t)} = jω·X(jω)  (derivative → multiply by jω)\n- Parseval: ∫|x(t)|²dt = (1/2π)∫|X(jω)|²dω"
    },
